        <div style="font-size: 20px; color: #0e1c42; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 10px;">For a few years, one cowboy could ride a hundred miles and never meet a fence. Then a twisted piece of wire changed the plains.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 18px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65;">The open range did not last. Within a generation, great ranches were fenced, bought by companies, and sometimes plowed under. You will meet the cattle barons who built huge ranches in Texas, see what barbed wire did, and see how the ranching world changed for the people who worked in it.</div>
